From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] avifil32: AVI files on the clipboard (6511)

AVIPutFileOnClipboard, AVIGetFromClipboard, AVIMakeStreamFromClipboard
and AVIClearClipboard were stubs. A file goes on the OLE clipboard as a
data object rendering its first video frame (CF_DIB) and its first
audio stream (CF_WAVE); this process gets the file itself back,
another process a file made of the clipboard's DIB and WAVE. DIBs and
WAVEs become editable streams. The AVI writer counted a sound stream
in blocks, so one write of many samples made a stream of one sample;
it counts samples now.
---
